.TH "TEXTTRACKCUE.EXIT_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
TextTrackCue.exit_event \- TextTrackCue: exit event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]exit\f[B]\f[R] event fires when a cue stops being active.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqexit\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onexit = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R] with no added properties.
.SH EXAMPLE
In the following example, \f[CR]cue\f[R] prints to the console when it
stops being displayed as the active cue.
.IP
.EX
cue.addEventListener(\(dqenter\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(dqCue 1 has left the building.\(dq);
});
.EE
